--- A field held as a growing int (Big), read through a record-or-none link, is typed
--- a 64-bit int: the compiled program does not build.
---
--- Interpreted (crow run -i): prints
---     1180591620717411303424
--- Compiled (crow run): the program does not build:
---     error[E0308]: mismatched types
---       --> src/main.rs:49:12
---     (rustc: expected `i64` because of return type, found `Int`)
---     error: the compiled program does not build — the Rust compiler refused what Crow
---     accepted, a bug in Crow, not in this program (`crow run -i` runs it meanwhile)
--- Expected: 1180591620717411303424, as interpreted.
---
--- `crow build --ir`:
---     struct Box { n: Big, next: OptRecord(Box) }
---     pure get(t: OptRecord(Box)) -> Int
---       return t.n
--- The read `t.n` of a link (`OptRecord`) is ranged as a 64-bit int while the field is
--- Big, and nothing converts it; the IR verifier lets it through. The same at the top
--- level: `x = c.next`, then `y = 0` / `y = x.n` is `let y: Int` assigned the Big field
--- (E0308). A field read of a plain record (`Record(Box)`) is Big and builds.
--- How it bites in practice (rosetta/avl_tree.co): a node keeping its height,
--- `Node[key, 1 + max[height_of[left], height_of[right]], left, right]` with
--- `height_of[t]` = 0 for none else `t.height` — the field grows through the cycle,
--- is settled Big, and `height_of` (its parameter a link) answers Int: no build.

struct Box [n, next]

fn get[t]
    return t.n

b = Box[2 ^ 70, 0]
c = Box[1, b]
log[get[c.next]]
